      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Nunda’s name comes from the Seneca word meaning “where the valley meets the hills,” reflecting its geography.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nunda%2C_New_York",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The large grinding wheel in the village pavilion was salvaged from the nearby Woodworth factory, a nod to local industrial heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nundahistory.org/walkingtour.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic building that now houses the Nunda Family Pharmacy was originally a bakery before being moved to its current spot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nundahistory.org/walkingtour.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town celebrated its 200th anniversary on March 11, 2008, marking two centuries of community life in Nunda.",
